1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,778
Welcome to Matrix. Matrix brings together people

2
00:00:02,818 --> 00:00:05,716
team members, AI resources and the devices you authorize

3
00:00:05,756 --> 00:00:08,601
to complete software development tasks with results you

4
00:00:08,641 --> 00:00:09,178
can verify.

5
00:00:09,918 --> 00:00:12,700
It solves a familiar problem. Command-line tools

6
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:15,699
APIs, accounts and devices are scattered everywhere

7
00:00:15,739 --> 00:00:18,640
so it's hard to know which resources actually work

8
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:21,815
how much quota is left, and what is running right now.

9
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:24,285
Matrix connects all of them in one system.

10
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:27,285
In Matrix, the Brain thinks and plans

11
00:00:27,325 --> 00:00:30,891
and can run in the cloud. The Hand is your own computer or

12
00:00:30,931 --> 00:00:34,310
server, and performs the real file and tool operations.

13
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:37,854
A Workspace is a project folder you explicitly authorize.

14
00:00:37,894 --> 00:00:41,149
Using a model and accessing files on a device are two

15
00:00:41,189 --> 00:00:42,454
separate permissions.

16
00:00:43,194 --> 00:00:45,312
Let's start with the Matrix desktop app.

17
00:00:45,352 --> 00:00:47,902
The Overview page shows whether you're signed in

18
00:00:47,942 --> 00:00:51,032
this device's connection, and whether the local gateway is

19
00:00:51,072 --> 00:00:52,866
running. Then step through Account

20
00:00:52,906 --> 00:00:55,510
Device and Gateway, AI Resources and Core Modules

21
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:57,830
to manage connections, discovered resources

22
00:00:57,870 --> 00:00:59,611
and core modules such as VL-Base.

23
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:03,068
In the browser, Matrix has just four main sections

24
00:01:03,108 --> 00:01:05,770
Pool, Task, Admin and Settings. Pool lists the AI

25
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:07,645
resources you're authorized to use

26
00:01:07,685 --> 00:01:09,740
with clear prices and remaining quota.

27
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:12,277
Resources are requested on demand and returned

28
00:01:12,317 --> 00:01:15,144
automatically after each round, with clear usage and

29
00:01:15,184 --> 00:01:15,751
accounting.

30
00:01:16,491 --> 00:01:19,295
On the Task page, pick a device at the top.

31
00:01:19,335 --> 00:01:22,800
The left side shows Workspaces, task lines and tasks.

32
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:25,115
The first time, click Add Workspace

33
00:01:25,155 --> 00:01:27,628
choose a project folder on that device

34
00:01:27,668 --> 00:01:29,149
and create a task line.

35
00:01:29,889 --> 00:01:32,390
Creating a task needs no complex dialogs.

36
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:35,365
The Assistant opens a task draft right in place.

37
00:01:35,405 --> 00:01:38,216
Write your goal, and choose how to collaborate

38
00:01:38,256 --> 00:01:40,261
a single agent, an AI leader team

39
00:01:40,301 --> 00:01:43,546
or managed by you. Then pick a predefined workflow or

40
00:01:43,586 --> 00:01:46,149
dynamic planning, and the model resources.

41
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:49,186
Click Send and start, and the task is created and

42
00:01:49,226 --> 00:01:49,744
launched.

43
00:01:50,484 --> 00:01:53,472
While a task runs, one run canvas shows participants

44
00:01:53,512 --> 00:01:56,441
workflow steps, feedback and real execution status.

45
00:01:56,481 --> 00:01:59,586
In a team task, the leader breaks down and reviews the

46
00:01:59,626 --> 00:02:02,672
work, and workers carry it out. The execution context

47
00:02:02,712 --> 00:02:05,933
tells you which model, device and Workspace handled each

48
00:02:05,973 --> 00:02:06,224
step.

49
00:02:06,964 --> 00:02:10,217
Workflow is a separate choice: no predefined workflow

50
00:02:10,257 --> 00:02:13,634
an existing static workflow, or dynamic planning by AI.

51
00:02:13,674 --> 00:02:16,056
A static workflow has a fixed topology.

52
00:02:16,096 --> 00:02:19,162
Dynamic planning first builds a plan from the goal

53
00:02:19,202 --> 00:02:22,455
and can propose controlled graph changes as new facts

54
00:02:22,495 --> 00:02:26,058
appear, with each new step, its reason and its scope shown

55
00:02:26,098 --> 00:02:28,729
on the graph. A step can also call an agent

56
00:02:28,769 --> 00:02:30,593
an AI team, or a sub-workflow.

57
00:02:31,333 --> 00:02:34,610
Here's a DAG run, step by step. The leader produces a

58
00:02:34,650 --> 00:02:38,176
plan. Steps whose dependencies are ready run in parallel.

59
00:02:38,216 --> 00:02:41,243
When testing finds a problem, a fix step is added

60
00:02:41,283 --> 00:02:44,684
dynamically. Nodes that need a human decision pause and

61
00:02:44,724 --> 00:02:47,375
wait for you. Then the result is delivered.

62
00:02:47,415 --> 00:02:50,942
On the real workflow canvas, every node shows live status

63
00:02:50,982 --> 00:02:54,383
done, runnable or paused. Open a node to see its inputs

64
00:02:54,423 --> 00:02:58,013
outputs and run details, and all artifacts are listed when

65
00:02:58,053 --> 00:02:59,077
the run finishes.

66
00:02:59,817 --> 00:03:02,454
In the same task area, you can open a terminal

67
00:03:02,494 --> 00:03:05,131
browse generated files and read detailed logs.

68
00:03:05,171 --> 00:03:08,506
Once delivered, results, tests and failure reasons are all

69
00:03:08,546 --> 00:03:11,416
traceable. A finished chat is not a finished task.

70
00:03:11,456 --> 00:03:13,162
Only verifiable results count.

71
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:15,594
You can stop a task at any time

72
00:03:15,634 --> 00:03:17,997
and Matrix confirms exactly what will stop.

73
00:03:18,037 --> 00:03:19,953
Failures, decisions waiting for you

74
00:03:19,993 --> 00:03:22,524
and waits for resources are all clearly shown.

75
00:03:22,564 --> 00:03:25,486
If a resource fails, Matrix can request an equivalent

76
00:03:25,526 --> 00:03:28,504
replacement within your authorized scope and continue.

77
00:03:28,544 --> 00:03:31,689
It never silently switches models or expands permissions.

78
00:03:32,429 --> 00:03:34,833
For companies, the owner creates an organization in

79
00:03:34,873 --> 00:03:37,613
Settings, invites members, and grants the company resource

80
00:03:37,653 --> 00:03:39,674
pool and device access to members or teams.

81
00:03:39,714 --> 00:03:42,118
Employees use company resources directly on company

82
00:03:42,158 --> 00:03:44,514
projects, returned automatically after each round.

83
00:03:44,554 --> 00:03:47,006
Company scheduling never borrows employees' personal

84
00:03:47,046 --> 00:03:47,485
resources.

85
00:03:48,225 --> 00:03:51,240
Next, VLC IDE, the VisualLogic development workbench.

86
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,833
Open a project, and one editor gives you flow

87
00:03:53,873 --> 00:03:55,850
code, theme, preview, visual, logic

88
00:03:55,890 --> 00:03:58,905
ER and database views, so UI, business logic and data

89
00:03:58,945 --> 00:04:00,864
models can all be edited visually.

90
00:04:01,604 --> 00:04:04,728
A built-in AI assistant lets you describe a new app

91
00:04:04,768 --> 00:04:06,712
workflow or component, or adjust

92
00:04:06,752 --> 00:04:09,1000
ask and diagnose. Then check and compile in one click

93
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,791
preview the result, and publish to the cloud.

94
00:04:12,831 --> 00:04:16,264
Flows, docs, skills and tools live in the same workbench

95
00:04:16,304 --> 00:04:19,055
and Build, Flow and Matrix share one runtime.

96
00:04:19,795 --> 00:04:23,136
You can also pick another authorized device in the browser

97
00:04:23,176 --> 00:04:25,117
and develop its projects remotely.

98
00:04:25,157 --> 00:04:28,439
The Brain plans in the cloud, while the Hand stays on the

99
00:04:28,479 --> 00:04:31,761
device where the project lives, reading and writing files

100
00:04:31,801 --> 00:04:34,967
and running commands through a restricted tool channel.

101
00:04:35,007 --> 00:04:37,240
Results flow back to the original task.

102
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:41,085
Sign in, add a Workspace, and describe your goal in the

103
00:04:41,125 --> 00:04:44,344
Assistant. Three steps, and AI completes real development

104
00:04:44,384 --> 00:04:46,346
work within the limits you control.

105
00:04:46,386 --> 00:04:48,576
Matrix: every execution, on the record.
